                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce2eef06-abd3-3d2f-a4e8-4045b0be33d9",
                        "entry_id": "9c78d3f1-695a-3921-ad8b-7d5590c9a78e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To put someone into a straitjacket."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literally"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12f29c64-3e44-49ae-ba20-619da7b243c3",
                                "sense_id": "ce2eef06-abd3-3d2f-a4e8-4045b0be33d9",
                                "text": "What he asked himself now was,—could Miss Edge and Miss Baker, in order to get him out of the house, have set Birt onto Elizabeth, be in league with the man to break a poor old fellow down by simply driving his sad girl out of her wits? To have her straitjacketted even, muffled in a padded room?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                        "entry_id": "9c78d3f1-695a-3921-ad8b-7d5590c9a78e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To restrict the freedom of, either physically or psychologically."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "042cea6b-25ca-48a0-8609-63327187c4e0",
                                "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                                "text": "Charles for five whole days in a Victorian topper and tailcoat when he practically had to be straitjacketted to get him into tails for a three-hour wedding?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a5d3651-6178-4180-8ab3-98b685386d94",
                                "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                                "text": "Encouraging, allowing for, and maintaining a plurality of viewpoints concerning public policy, for instance, adaptively (even though partially and incompletely) reduces the chances of a rigidly deterministic and reductionistic mindset maladaptively straitjacketting our abilities to deal with dynamic complexity and to appreciate the benefits of malleability and self-criticality in remaining open to the challenges of our environment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96e7f470-a20c-48ed-90c2-fd7409fc2a15",
                                "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                                "text": "But it has not always been like this. The last time human remains hit the headlines occurred when the government-sponsored Palmer Report was published. It was deeply antagonistic to research on human remains, and recommended straitjacketing archaeological research within the same framework as medical science."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a788cb87-160f-4816-bcb3-b604fdd5efb2",
                                "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                                "text": "Where most primates have a respectable pair of grasping rear hands we have two changelings: long arched pads with rounded chins at one end and stumpy thumbs straight-jacketed to baby fingers at the other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe139531-88e6-4a7a-b600-a15fffb4b4b6",
                                "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                                "text": "she couldnʼt wait to go to college, have a career and leave her parentsʼ straitjacketed lives behind"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c8fa98c-4c19-49e3-88cd-0158ea5c3cd0",
                                "sense_id": "63241a02-aadf-3602-b192-25bebdb40f19",
                                "text": "A Labour opposition that has straitjacketed its pledges and ambitions with its fears of blowing its strongest chance in years to gain power."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "16dcbc95-50b5-40d9-a176-dfa3d10aeaa0",
                        "source_entry_id": "9c78d3f1-695a-3921-ad8b-7d5590c9a78e",
                        "source_sense_description": "to put someone into a straitjacket",
                        "target_lang_word": "iemand een dwangbuis aandoen",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99da4427-52cf-4c42-9123-c1aa05cb7189",
                        "source_entry_id": "9c78d3f1-695a-3921-ad8b-7d5590c9a78e",
                        "source_sense_description": "to put someone into a straitjacket",
                        "target_lang_word": "camisole de force",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "camisole de force",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00fe5297-f833-3f7b-8be7-1883d0d59553",
                                        "entry_id": "fa1eef81-a282-3dfb-8c87-01a015173ada",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Camisole à manches bouclées par-derrière qu’on mettait quelquefois à des aliénés, à des prisonniers pour leur ôter l’usage de leurs bras et les empêcher de se blesser ou de frapper ceux qui les approchent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Prison"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "858961fe-a9c8-4713-887f-900ed8debc8c",
                                                "sense_id": "00fe5297-f833-3f7b-8be7-1883d0d59553",
                                                "text": "Des femmes sont enfermées là, les bras serrés, la poitrine écrasée par une camisole de force."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cebe4756-8d44-4363-82b4-7616046cd67a",
                                                "sense_id": "00fe5297-f833-3f7b-8be7-1883d0d59553",
                                                "text": "Troppmann devait se déshabiller. Deux gardiens s’approchèrent de lui et commencèrent à lui enlever sa camisole de force, sorte de blouse de toile bleue grossière, avec des courroies et des boucles, avec de longues manches en sac, du bout desquelles descendaient des ficelles fortes serrées autour des reins et vers la taille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15fbbfc5-9161-4ec8-8a20-48129833c9f7",
                                                "sense_id": "00fe5297-f833-3f7b-8be7-1883d0d59553",
                                                "text": "C'était un homme rouge, jovial, à la fois parce que la fréquentation de la déchéance nerveuse ne l'empêchait pas d'être très bien portant mais aussi pour rassurer ses malades par le gros rire de son bonjour et de son au revoir, quitte à aider de ses bras d'athlète à leur passer plus tard la camisole de force."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32cb2701-dc63-4521-ab28-90dc62cd8b4a",
                                                "sense_id": "00fe5297-f833-3f7b-8be7-1883d0d59553",
                                                "text": "Ce n’est pas une solution que de passer à la nature une camisole de force, car elle la met en pièces, comme Samson les liens fragiles dont on le chargeait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90f2466d-fe58-4224-b4ae-caf8666cc5a8",
                                                "sense_id": "00fe5297-f833-3f7b-8be7-1883d0d59553",
                                                "text": "Le docteur était aux petits soins, et aux gros médocs. Tous les jours, son sbire en blouse blanche me piquousait et me faisait avaler des cachetons pour faire bonne mesure. Camisole chimique, que ça s'appelle. La camisole de force emprisonne le corps, la chimique enchaîne l'esprit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "687c1cea-859a-4803-b40d-a16d32e54a6d",
                        "source_entry_id": "9c78d3f1-695a-3921-ad8b-7d5590c9a78e",
